# Turnstile {DASH} build plan (2026-10-06)

Intent: a small turn counter for the bench rig, so one bench session reports its turns.
Constraints: Python 3.9 standard library only; the check runs through `sh checks/unit.sh`.
Out of scope: a web dashboard

## Slice A {DASH} the counter
Goal: the counter counts turns and resets to zero.
Requirements:
- R1: a turn adds one to the count
- R2: a reset sets the count back to zero
Acceptance criteria:
- AC1: two turns read 2 (verify: a test in tests/test_turnstile.py)
- AC2: a reset after two turns reads 0 (verify: a test in tests/test_turnstile.py)
Footprint: `src/turnstile.py`, `tests/`
Checks:
- unit: sh checks/unit.sh
Not in this slice: the encoder
Depends on: nothing
Status: not started

